    skos:definition "articles coated or varnished with lacquer, which stand the effect of washing well. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 232]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (group=grp_glass_ceramics_paper_woodware; processing_state=manufactured): Named manufactured sundry (furniture, bedding, printed matter, jewellery, plated and ceramic wares, pianos) left in the residual bin. Layer-1 observations: 13 rows, 1827–1851. Series: KEW_CUST 4 ×13. Units: (no unit) ×13. Top routes: Canada → England ×13."@en ;
